      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loxahatchee_Groves%2C_Florida",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After the West Palm Beach Canal opened in 1917, Bensel envisioned a waterfront farming community along its banks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loxahatchee_Groves%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 1928 Okeechobee hurricane devastated Loxahatchee Groves, knocking almost every home off its foundations.",
